            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous rupture of renal angiomyolipoma. Report of three cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>345-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The presentation of renal angiomyolipoma as an acute abdominal condition, together with hypovolemic shock, is very rare. 3 such cases are described herein with special reference to the diagnostic problems and recommended management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
